4403653c89\neo -\u003e d01d2fc50a18\nes-CL -\u003e 70c69d72a169\neu -\u003e 1f932419db5c\nfr -\u003e 91ae44453340\nfy-NL -\u003e 40dae758d93f\nhe -\u003e f7c9e49593d8\nnl -\u003e 6fbe1410ee7c\nrm -\u003e 38662bd46166", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4e29d2291bc8e48944b00c2f6e624101a8edf6eb", "parents": ["2e6c3c84b0e79c3c86afc2e7032d926ccb4fc6d9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1568026830, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "313": {"changesets": [{"author": "L10n Bumper Bot \u003crelease+l10nbumper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nit -\u003e cb3c178edc0e\nko -\u003e d7dda637abd0\nsl -\u003e 76b63367878e", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6a6ead415dc00961103391b1cbef195c956ac8a6", "parents": ["4e29d2291bc8e48944b00c2f6e624101a8edf6eb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1568030430, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "314": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D45183", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "781722aef76db2494607dcb3cc8b5d03bfcbbc86", "parents": ["6a6ead415dc00961103391b1cbef195c956ac8a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1566180 - Update Widevine fallback downloader to 4.10.1440.19. r=rhelmer a=RyanVM\n\nUpdate the fallback downloader to make sure it's in step with balrog rules.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D39828", "files": ["toolkit/content/gmp-sources/widevinecdm.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7055fd88e65dc73960e23e5f26c6918b0fdddbb7", "parents": ["781722aef76db2494607dcb3cc8b5d03bfcbbc86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1563640 - Swiftkey keyboard doesn't work correctly on textboxes. r=snorp, a=RyanVM\n\nThis issue is race condition of Gecko thread and InputConnection thread.\n\nWhen inputting `[ENTER]` in VKB, Switftkey generates keyboard event (down and up), then set empty span to current position.\n\nIt means that the following occurs.\n\n1. Inserting CR by [ENTER] key event of Swiftkey.\n2. Swiftkey sets empty span with current selection position. Then GV sets new selection with it due to adding span.\n3. By 1., text and selection are updated, then GV receives new selection position by 1.\n4. Selection notification by 2. is received, then selection is back to previous position unfortunately.\n\nAlthough we should use 1 and 3's selection, GV uses 4's selection since this is last notification. But 2's selection is current selection until we don't update text. So it is unnecessary to set same selection again by 2.\n\nAlso, most IMEs don't send key event by 1, and they replace with new text without 1 and 2 So this issue occurs on Switftkey only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D40926", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoEditable.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "55ce33264266e4b3cd4972fa03b783542a7619a7", "parents": ["7055fd88e65dc73960e23e5f26c6918b0fdddbb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1572728 - Sync Gecko's selection for sendKey test of testInputConnection. r=snorp, a=RyanVM\n\nActually, `assertTextAndSelectionAt` checks Java side text and selection only.\nSo even if `assertTextAndSelectionAt` is successful, Gecko's text and selection\naren't updated yet. Since `sendKeyEvent` test uses both Gecko's selection and\nJava's selection, this has timing issue. Since `sendKeyEvent` uses Gecko's\nselection for insertion point, we have to sync Java's selection with Gecko's\nselection. But since there is no way to sync it, this sendKey test may be failure.\n\nTo sync both data, this test should always use key event to update both Gecko\nside and Java side correctly. GV's test uses Gecko's selection, so this issue\nis robocop test only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D42599", "files": ["mobile/android/tests/browser/robocop/src/org/mozilla/gecko/tests/testInputConnection.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f2b71af2c5ebda5fab9e0b7bcf0e4e6c2d5ced2a", "parents": ["55ce33264266e4b3cd4972fa03b783542a7619a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Henning \u003cjh+bugzilla@buttercookie.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1577612 - Support functional CSS color syntax in themes. r=snorp, a=RyanVM\n\nA lot/most? webextension static themes use this way to specify colours.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D44208", "files": ["mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/lwt/LightweightTheme.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "585151cfc057abfd6b4f709cff49d9434e6988b5", "parents": ["f2b71af2c5ebda5fab9e0b7bcf0e4e6c2d5ced2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1578614 - Change Fennec about:addons' AMO URL from \"firefox\" to \"android\"; r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D44768", "files": ["mobile/android/app/mobile.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "37ec6a002816ffa36f0b91ff0061bc4b5bc43004", "parents": ["585151cfc057abfd6b4f709cff49d9434e6988b5"], "tags": ["FENNEC_68_2b2_BUILD1", "FENNEC_68_2b2_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1568035187, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "315": {"changesets": [{"author": "Geoff Lankow \u003cgeoff@darktrojan.net\u003e", "branch": "THUNDERBIRD_68_VERBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1529205 - Remove DateTimePickerParent's dependency on gBrowser; r=mconley a=jorgk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D35392", "files": ["browser/base/content/tabbrowser.js", "browser/modules/FormValidationHandler.jsm", "toolkit/content/widgets/browser-custom-element.js", "toolkit/modules/DateTimePickerParent.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "db4f8b58bf16e6737ac31e115a9bb4f8e4b68945", "parents": ["80a61871ecfd082792b39ca68d3632fd334e91ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos Alvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "THUNDERBIRD_68_VERBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1561288 - Don't override currentContent when focusing something on a shadow root. r=smaug a=jorgk DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nIt is wrong, what we're trying to focus is frame-\u003eGetContent() still.\n\nThis is not reproducible outside of Thunderbird because for it to happen the\nfocus manager needs to wrap around the start content.\n\nHere's what's going on:\n\n * We start with a \u003ctree\u003e focused, which is a shadow host.\n * There's nothing else to focus inside the \u003ctree\u003e, or after the \u003ctree\u003e in document order.\n * So we restart the search with a different tabindex (1), but find nothing before the tree (since all focusable elements before the tree also have tabindex 0), and we return wrongly in [1], instead of searching with tabindex 0 again afterwards. (Since the child frame is not focusable, we wrongly end up at [1], and returning early, since currentContent != frame-\u003eGetContent(), instead of keeping looking for the right thing to focus.)\n\nAs I said this cannot reproduce on content, as far as I can tell, so I'm not\nsure how to go about testing this, but all the shadow dom tab navigation tests\nkeep passing with this change.\n\n[1]: https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/06bd14ced96f25ff1dbd5352cb985fc0fa12a64e/dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp#3560\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36196", "files": ["dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f0c0729a02198b423b995f2873adac7cb0b96435", "parents": ["db4f8b58bf16e6737ac31e115a9bb4f8e4b68945"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Nguyen \u003cntim.bugs@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "THUNDERBIRD_68_VERBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1563529 - Make HTML inputs inherit font in global.css. r=dao a=jorgk DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D36933", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/global.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3099f60b0774651728a6f9a142b6896327b8bd2", "parents": ["f0c0729a02198b423b995f2873adac7cb0b96435"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "THUNDERBIRD_68_VERBRANCH", "desc": "Close old TB68 verbranch head. a=npotb DONTBUILD", "files": [], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "16f460bc714e1f7554392d86aca9741c15ef4683", "parents": ["e3099f60b0774651728a6f9a142b6896327b8bd2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1568049768, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "316": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_68_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Close obsolete FIREFOX_ESR_68_0_X_RELBRANCH. a=release", "files": [], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9e799a98480d7eeed18e45494ec6396b04d4f770", "parents": ["e8533b58596eb308d04f3dafc6f1b1a127f984f6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1568052627, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "317": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_68_1_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "No bug - Bump version number to 68.1.1. a=release DONTBUILD", "files": ["browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone